[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3311432896","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3311432896","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3311432896,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FYHTA","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T09:26:10Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T09:26:10Z","body":"> ERROR: modules/navigation/3d/nav_map_builder_3d.cpp:151 - Navigation map synchronization error. Attempted to merge a navigation mesh polygon edge with another already-merged edge.\n\nYou already had the layout error in Godot 4.4.1 and did not fix it, so now it is just back to haunt you in different form in Godot 4.5.\n\n\nThe processing order of edges has shifted because regions now merge first before the map. So you still have the same broken navmesh edge in your layout but now it just happens that a more important polygon gets not connected so you notice it more.\n\nIf the cause of that error is just tiny edges sprinkeled over the layout you can go to the ProjectSettings and set `navigation/2d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale` to a smaller value. If the error does not go away even with the smallest value possible you have some navmesh overlap created somewhere.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3311432896/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3311457039","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3311457039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3311457039,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FYNMP","user":{"login":"Neonxxx","id":78502559,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NTAyNTU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78502559?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx","html_url":"https://github.com/Neonxxx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Neonxxx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T09:34:18Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T09:34:18Z","body":"thank you so much.\nsetting this setting: `navigation/2d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale` to the lowest possible value fixed my problem and thanks for the quick reply.\nmaybe it would have been good to set the value for `navigation/2d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale` to the lowest per default thought to avoid such problems in the future? \n\nBR","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3311457039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3311479391","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3311479391","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3311479391,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FYSpf","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T09:41:57Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T09:41:57Z","body":"> maybe it would have been good to set the value for navigation/2d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale to the lowest per default thought to avoid such problems in the future?\n\nThis will give projects float precision errors depending on their layout and size, hence why it is not auto set to the lowest value.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3311479391/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3311872999","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3311872999","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3311872999,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FZyvn","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T11:41:07Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T11:48:55Z","body":"I would also recommend to simplify the geometry that you use for the baking here in that level layout.\n\nYou seem to use a lot of circle shapes and those create very ugly navmesh layouts because their \"round\" shape forces 12 new edges around them which is a lot. Those force navmesh polygon splits which in turn cause many long and thin edges to appear everywhere. Try to replace them with a simpler shapes that have less edges, like a convex shape with just 3-8 edges. That alone will automatically give you a far cleaner navmesh layout when baked with better path query performance and path follow quality.\n\nAlso some of the wall sections seem to have collision shape artifacts, there is no reason why there should be so many new navmesh edges when baked there. That only happens when the baked collision shape of the tilemap does not line up, so go back to the tileset editor and make sure that you have snapping enabled and your collision polygon is as clean and simple as possible.\n\nThose things might as well be the reason why you have this error in the first place when some of them create tiny mini polygons.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3311872999/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312601402","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3312601402","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3312601402,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fckk6","user":{"login":"Ayuroo","id":230040131,"node_id":"U_kgDODbYiQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230040131?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo","html_url":"https://github.com/Ayuroo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T15:16:06Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T15:16:23Z","body":"I have the same issue in 3D. My geometry for the navmesh generation is already as simple as it can be (simple collision shapes with simple navigation obstacles that carve/cut the navmesh) yet it also produces the same error.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312601402/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312671948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3312671948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3312671948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fc1zM","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T15:35:25Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T15:35:25Z","body":"@Ayuroo Did you try lowering the 3d equivalent `navigation/3d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale` in the ProjectSettings? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312671948/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312922050","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3312922050","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3312922050,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fdy3C","user":{"login":"Ayuroo","id":230040131,"node_id":"U_kgDODbYiQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230040131?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo","html_url":"https://github.com/Ayuroo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ayuroo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-19T16:45:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-19T16:47:05Z","body":"Lowering it to a lower values seems to fix the issue, but it definitely feels like a hacky workaround to an issue, that wasn't as impacting before.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3312922050/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3316031722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3316031722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3316031722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FpqDq","user":{"login":"ElekKartofelek","id":6129332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMjkzMzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6129332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek","html_url":"https://github.com/ElekKartofelek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-21T14:30:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T14:30:46Z","body":"In my case 4.5 absolutely broke the whole 3D navigation workflow in my project. Navigation in 4.4.1 worked perfectly fine. Even though there were some \"More than 2 edges\" errors during baking NPCs were still able to navigate each terrain every single time. With new implementation pathfinding is straight up broken altogether if the same error happens.\n\nI understand these checks are there for a reason and should be handled and not ignored but fixing level geometry isn't really possible when  **terrain and structures are all procedurally generated**. It really feels like a huge step backwards.\n\nSetting `navigation/3d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale` even to the lowest value possible did not help in my case so I guess I'm stuck with 4.4 🥴","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3316031722/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3316516366","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3316516366","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3316516366,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FrgYO","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T02:05:48Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T02:05:48Z","body":"If you have tried all the other solutions and can't solve it yourself create and share an MRP.\n\n> I understand these checks are there for a reason and should be handled and not ignored but fixing level geometry isn't really possible when terrain and structures are all procedurally generated.\n\nThat is only one side to approach the problem, the other is to find a cell size + merge_rasterizer_cell_scale and bake settings that works with the procedural geometry. Especially in 3D there are a lot of bake settings that directly affect how easy it is to end up with a good (enough) navmesh or a cursed version of navmesh that has tiny bake artifact polygons all over the place that commonly cause such merge issues.\n\n> Setting navigation/3d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale even to the lowest value possible did not help in my case\n\nAt the lowest value the rasterization grid has a tiny cell size of 0.01. It is next to impossible to cause such issues in a natural way with such a tiny cell size except for when there is geometry overlap of navmesh. Overlap is an error in the navmesh placement and can't be fixed with settings, only by moving the faulty placed navmesh objects out of the way.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3316516366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3319183344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3319183344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3319183344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F1rfw","user":{"login":"foohines","id":4998620,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTg2MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4998620?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines","html_url":"https://github.com/foohines","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T13:53:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T13:53:03Z","body":"Here's a MRP that shows the same or a similar issue, and doesn't raise any errors during navmesh baking or runtime.\n\nIt works fine in 4.4.1, but not in 4.5\n\nSetting the merge_rasterizer_cell_scale to the lowest value had no effect.\n\n\n**Repo**: https://github.com/foohines/godot-4.5-navigation-bug\n\n**Zip** [godot-4.5-navigation-bug-main.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22467611/godot-4.5-navigation-bug-main.zip)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/34a7fac5-2575-40a9-a61d-2d0a860a19d9","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3319183344/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3319976910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3319976910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3319976910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F4tPO","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T16:14:08Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T16:14:08Z","body":"@foohines That project suffers from float precision problems because it uses extremely long and thin polygon edges. Layouts like this need to be broken up with chunks or other geometry. You can't have thin polygon edges that basically near overlap each other and then go over giant distances. That will always create problems and is unrelated to the issue here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3319976910/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320084487","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3320084487","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3320084487,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7F5HgH","user":{"login":"foohines","id":4998620,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTg2MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4998620?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines","html_url":"https://github.com/foohines","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/foohines/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-22T16:36:19Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T16:36:58Z","body":"@smix8 Thanks for your insight. \n\n1. Is it not still relevant that it works in 4.4.1 and breaks in 4.5? \n\n2. Should the engine throw the overlapping error in this case too? \n\n3. The region is around 4600x4600 pixels with the narrowest polygon due to a 15px gap near the center of the region.  What are appropriate chunk sizes for this situation to avoid float precision errors? ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3320084487/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323406788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3323406788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3323406788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GFynE","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T10:32:13Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T10:38:49Z","body":"@foohines On closer look there seem to be something going on with that specific 2d path post-processing. So unrelated to this very issue here but still its own thing that needs to be looked at.\n\nIn general what I wrote about thin and long edges still stands, but here I shrunk the size of the demo and still had the issue in some case. So I now overlayed both 2d and 3d with the same geometry and options. 3D works without issues and 2D does without that specific path postprocessing. They create the exact same paths, so there is something fishy going on in the 2d postprocessing. Possibly from the change to a dedicated NavigationServer2D that converted a lot of 3d code to 2d. Should create a dedicated issue for it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3323406788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325849456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3325849456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3325849456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GPG9w","user":{"login":"ElekKartofelek","id":6129332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMjkzMzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6129332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek","html_url":"https://github.com/ElekKartofelek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T23:15:56Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T23:15:56Z","body":"Here's a MRP with an example of a 3D terrain generated during runtime, saved to the scene and cleaned up. No matter the settings it still produces an error.\n\nKey difference:\n- In 4.4.1 pathfinding would work perfectly fine even after an error.\n- In 4.5 NavigationAgent3D is stuck to the closest NavigationMesh polygon it was spawned on\n\nHere's what it looks like:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2f5a8184-9f33-4f1a-90a5-b22700b9f6f7)\n\n[navigation-baking-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22503287/navigation-baking-bug.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3325849456/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327084609","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3327084609","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3327084609,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GT0hB","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T07:57:24Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T07:57:24Z","body":"@ElekKartofelek This is due to edge merge errors with the navmesh. In Godot 4.5 these errors are treated as actual errors, because they are. But that also means that in Godot 4.5 when such errors occurred it did no longer try to merge remaining edges because the error returned the function. PR should solve that https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110841","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327084609/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327328396","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110686#issuecomment-3327328396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110686","id":3327328396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7GUwCM","user":{"login":"ElekKartofelek","id":6129332,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMjkzMzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6129332?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek","html_url":"https://github.com/ElekKartofelek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ElekKartofelek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T09:05:25Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T09:09:57Z","body":"> [@ElekKartofelek](https://github.com/ElekKartofelek) In Godot 4.5 these errors are treated as actual errors, because they are.\n\nI understand that fully. I tried everything **not** to produce such errors and I experimented with all possible objects that are spawned in the world but then I realized the terrain itself is the problem. So then I tried getting just the terrain to work so I:\n- tripple checked if the mesh isn't generating any overlapping geometry (which is just a `PlaneMesh` with additional y offsets)\n- checked if baking `NavigationMesh` up to 5000m away from the center could cause the issue\n- tried lowering the resolution of the terrain\n- tried adjusting `navigation/3d/merge_rasterizer_cell_scale` to bare minimum and also `cell_height` and `cell_width` up to 1.0\n\nI still couldn't get it to work. I was fully on the _\"there must something I don't understand\"_ mindset while researching all the collisions of spawnable objects but that mentality was shattered the moment I couldn't get just a plane with uniformly offset vertices (excluding y axis) to work. Overlaps just aren't possible in this scenario, right?\n\n> PR should solve that https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110841\n\nI tried it already and it does resolve the issue of pathfinding. I'm so happy to see it also gives more insight about an error and how to mitigate it but even with that help I feel there's something wrong. I just can't seem to be able to find a proper way to handle my use case of navigation.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3327328396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]